From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, user32, uxtheme: Windows 7's themed menus

Purpose: draw the menu bar and popup menus of the Windows 7 shell
session as Windows 7 does.
Windows behavior (measured on Windows 7 SP1 with
tests/menu-theme-layout.c through public APIs and screenshots): a
version 4 visual style's Menu class draws the bar's background, the
pushed bar item, the popup's border, background and gutter, the hot
item, the check mark on its background, the submenu arrow and the
separator. While the window is active and no menu is open, the bar
item under the mouse is drawn with MENU_BARITEM's hot state; an
inactive window's bar has no hot item and gray text (109,109,109).
A popup item is as tall as the check background (22 with
Aero), a separator the separator part and the item margins (8); the
text starts after the gutter and the background's border size; the
shortcuts start 33 pixels after the longest text and end 19 pixels
before the item's end. Menu bar items fill the bar's 20 pixels from
its top. With keyboard cues off, access keys are underlined only while
the menu is used from the keyboard; DrawText's DT_HIDEPREFIX drops the
underscore.
Wine before: XP's flat menus, with no hot bar item and the active text
color in inactive windows; DT_HIDEPREFIX was ignored.
Change: a MenuTheme user32 callback asks Wine's uxtheme
(Win4WineMenuTheme) for the part sizes and margins and has it draw
the parts; win32u lays the menus out with them and draws the text;
the keyboard menu mode shows the access keys; user32's DrawText honors
DT_HIDEPREFIX. DefWindowProc's WM_NCMOUSEMOVE and WM_NCMOUSELEAVE follow
the bar item under the mouse (TME_NONCLIENT | TME_LEAVE) and redraw it
with MBI_HOT or MBI_DISABLEDHOT; selecting a bar item clears it. An
inactive bar's items use the disabled text color.
Evidence: a test window's menus, opened with Alt+F, left with Esc and
opened with the mouse, match Windows 7's at the same place to the
pixel apart from ClearType's colors; w7cmp.exe's menu bar with the
mouse over an item of the active window and of an inactive one is the
same as Windows 7's apart from the known glyph differences.
Scope: opted-in external shell with a version 4 style that has the
popup menu parts (Windows 7's Aero); XP's and ReactOS's styles keep
the current menus.
